Hmmm..... what do i think about this game
I FOCKIN LOVE IT (not.........kinda?)
I played this game for the customization and the cars ( i love cars, i spend half of my playtime drifting.)
This game has a REVOLUTIONARY customization system, need for speed barely come close. pffft, and you though that game was cool! (but yea, we dont have the capacity for infinite decals....that kinda sucks.) I mean, you can create your own decals if you dont love the stuff you get, but guess how you make your decals? you use the game's! using squares, triangles, and hundreds of other shapes, you can create masterpeices you can stick on yourself and your vehicles! using the huge amount of clothes and stuff, you can make your character look any way you want him to look! (Some items and such may require alot more playtime to unlock then others, though.) Cars though, may be alot harder to unlock, and even harder to customize, because you get such a small decal limit to work with as a free-to-play.
This game.........is free to play, you only get one permanent weapon in the game other the the starter one, which you actually get to choose pretty early on in the game....... the problem with choosing one weapon early on in the game is, though.... you dont know which weapon fits your playstyle or even which playstyle your even comfortable with! me, personally... i chose a sniper rifle which i thought was a one shot... it did not work out, i hate the playstyle i have to take with that weapon. that and the fact that the sniper rifle was not a one shot kill, the stats can look so deceiving, but in truth isn't a one-shot-ANYTHING weapon in this game.
The game is pay to win, yes. But personally, i got what i wanted and came to this game for, so im happy, TAKE INTO CONSIDERATION THAT I HAVE NOT SPENT A DIME ON THIS GAME. Actually, i have spend a dime.. 200 dimes... you know what that did?? nothing. i spend my 20 dollars expecting in-game currency (G1C, also known as G1 credits.) and what came out?? nothing... and nothing apeared on my purchase history, either!. so thats 20 bucks down the drain.
The benifits of becoming a premium member and spending money on this game are really nice, though. so dont be scared to borrow mum's wallet with the intention to spend 10 dollars on a game where you run over innocent civilians and kill people mericlessly :D. Becoming a premium member can bring enourmous customization oppurtunities, allowing you to fit so many more decals on yourself and your car! Also, if you do spend money on G1C, you must get a gun from the armas marketplace before doing ANYTHING ELSE. but beware, some guns on there are utter crap, too. so do research and pick the correct gun, so you dont waste your prescious money..
to those of you people who dont want to spend money on this game, if you are smart with money... REAL SMART with money(in-game currency, of course.), you can have the cool cars and the cool payed weapons that everyone else has, throuth the use of an in-game community marketplace. the problem is, of course, is that you cannot customize stuff you buy off other players, so i reccomend chatting with car designers to purchas something off them that they can tailor to your wants! my 190 hours and my current status say something, though...i have couple cool cars that make drifters, but i am nowhere CLOSE to getting a payed weapon... i dont see myself ever getting one.
If you are new to the game you can always contact me in-game (Lolfungreg for enforcers of LFGames for criminals) and i can help guide you through the game and hopefuly halp you gain a good amount of revenue. just hope i am online.
Oh yea! I forgot to Talk about the refer-a-freind program....... That is actually one of the only good bits of the game. It pretty obvious how it goes.
]Send a bud your email
]Your bud will then make an account and character through that emal
]You play missions together and help your bud finish tutorials
]Look in the refer a freind page, to see what points you have. (You of course gain points by playing with your freind and helping him finish tutorials)
] You can then gain FREE acces to premium and paid-only Weapons, Exclusive cars and Bodykits, Weapon skins, and Clothing using your points :D.
The refer-a-freind program REALLY benifited me through this game, and in the end actually really brought me back into APB. Give it a try, see how you like it!

